WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer FIFTY real snapchats from real snapchatters.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.000
Let's get right to it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.020
"Favorite thing about Indianapolis?" Race day!

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:14.420
"Favorite TV show?" The Americans, not just the best show about spies on TV, also the best show about marriage on TV.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.620
"How are the puff levels?" A little too high, actually, hold on. Yeah, that's better.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.480
"Any great movies to recommend?" I really love both 'Dope', and 'The End of the Tour'.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.560
"Why do you love writing?" For me, it's like the number one way of escaping the prison of my consciousness.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.280
"Biggest lesson from the refugee camps?" I'd never really considered the horror of dislocation, like, it's one thing to

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.660
experience trauma inside your community, and in a social structure you understand.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.940
But it's totally different to experience loss in a place that isn't yours, surrounded by people you don't know.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.700
"Where do you see yourself in ten years?" I don't know, but I know what I wanna be doing on Tuesdays.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:51.020
"Favorite YA debut of 2016?" It hasn't come out yet, but 'Spontaneous' is the best book about spontaneous combustion you will ever read.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.460
"Hints about your new book?" Uh, it concerns the White River.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.340
"When's it gonna come out?" I dunno, not this year.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:03.360
"What do you think of Hamilton?" It's just so astonishingly good, it's so nuanced, and rich, and the songs are so catchy!

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.640
"Favorite Hamilton song?" That's like asking me to pick between my kids, but I am pretty fond of the cabinet meeting rap battles.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:14.360
"Can you name a character in your new book Avery?" No! I can't just, like, choose- actually, y'know, I kinda like that name. Maybe.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.500
"How many Katherines qualifies as an abundance?" Mmm, nineteen, possibly eighteen.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.600
What was your childhood best friend's name?" Yeah, no, that adorable puppy filter is not going to trick me,

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.860
person-who-is-clearly-trying-to-learn-the-answer-to-my-security-questions.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.480
"What was your dream job as a kid?" Earthworm scientist.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.300
"How would you get away with murder?" Well, given that 40% of murders in Indianapolis go unsolved, it's apparently not that difficult.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.100
"Favorite piece of furniture?" This La-Z-Boy, in which I've written at least part of all my books,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.540
and which was described by The New Yorker as, quote, "grubby," and, quote, "oatmeal-colored,"

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:48.520
and by The Wall Street Journal as, quote, "tan." That's right, my La-Z-Boy's been covered by some of America's finest periodicals,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.120
and yet, does La-Z-Boy send me recliners for free? No they don't.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.200
"Should I read 'The Fountainhead'?" But there are so many GOOD books.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.000
"What's your opinion on sporks?" I guess I just feel like they're not very good at two things.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.820
"Honest opinion on Donald Trump?" I'm reminded of something Cyrus Ching once said: "Never wrestle with a pig. You get filthy, and besides, the pig likes it."

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.840
"What's you favorite reading position?" This.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.400
"Do you write with music or in silence?" Usually silence, occasionally The Mountain Goats.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.400
"Band you most listen to?" Definitely The Mountain Goats, followed by Hank Green and the Perfect Strangers.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.100
"Favorite Hank song?" Strange Charm.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:26.620
"Who the eff is Hank?" Hank is a young adult novel published in 2005. Unfortunately, I have no control over the movie rights to Hank.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.540
"Any news on the Looking For Alaska movie?" Sadly, no.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.040
"Thoughts on Dr. Who?" I am very excited for the new spinoff series written by my friend Patrick Ness.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.560
"Have you ever shaved your head?" Yeah, in high school I shaved my head, and then when it started to grow back,

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.460
I dyed my hair fuchsia-plum,  but I had a really bad reaction to the hair dye. So I ended up

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.040
with a lot of fuchsia-plum dandruff. Oh, and I was so stressed out about my fuchsia-plum dandruff.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.720
I'm so glad I'm not in high school anymore.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.100
"What is this?" I believe that's a sloth, who, having eaten too much oversized lollipop, is now barfing a rainbow.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.580
"How do I survive reading 'Macbeth'?" I think you have a much better chance of surviving it than Macbeth does.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.700
"Favorite tree?" I guess former Orlando Magic player Tree Rollins.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.760
"Favourite season?" Oh, definitely Season Kent, the music supervisor for the The Fault In Our Stars and Paper Towns movies.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.340
"Favourite dad joke?" I'm pretty fond of the ones I just told.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.820
"Are you making a cooking channel?" Maybe!

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.840
"Monopoly or Scrabble?" Scrabble.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.060
"How's Willy?" He's so good! Willy, say 'hi'. He can't, he can't talk.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:24.180
"We're newlyweds! How do we build a strong marriage?" My parents gave us two words of advice that have been very helpful: 'mutual generosity'.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.040
"Can you speak Spanish?" No. Well, except I guess I just did.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.680
"If you could speak any language, what would it be?" Probably Spanish.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.180
"Did you have braces?"  Yes, for three years.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.020
"Coke or Pepsi?" Diet Dr. Pepper.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.880
"Dinosaurs or dragons?" Dinos.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.480
"Favorite infinity?" Real numbers.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.480
"Is there gonna be more CrashCourse with you?" Yes, more literature this summer, we're reading all these books.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.700
"What are you reading right now?" This, it's so good!

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.540
"Feelings on socks?" I love them!

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.200
"How excited are you for VidCon?" Very, less than ninety days to go.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.240
"Llamas or alpacas?" Llamas.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:58.220
"What's your Starbucks order?" Uh, can I just have, like a, like a regular, just a large regular coffee? Just, just, black coffee? Thank you.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.120
Fifty questions in four minutes! Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

